//! Incremental APFS copy-on-write macOS ARM64 (`aarch64-apple-darwin`) Mach-O linker
//! (`MachOIncremental`).
//!
//! # When to use
//! Call [`linkOrPatch`] in dev and test builds of pure-Silk Apple Silicon executables (`--backend
//! direct`, `--optimization none`). On the initial build, [`MachOLink.linkWithOptions`] emits an
//! incremental-ready `MH_EXECUTE` binary with 12-byte fixed Silk call thunks, padded function
//! slots, `__TEXT,__text`/`__TEXT,__const`/`__DATA,__data` headroom, pre-allocated
//! `LC_DYLD_CHAINED_FIXUPS` page-start slots covering all `__DATA` headroom pages, pure-Silk
//! ad-hoc SHA-256 `LC_CODE_SIGNATURE`, and a compact `<output>.machostate` v2 sidecar.
//!
//! # Details
//! On subsequent rebuilds:
//! - Raw `AArch64Object` (`\0a64`) chunks are scanned and hashed with 128-bit SipHash-1-3 without
//!   decoding; unchanged chunks are skipped in `O(dirty)` time.
//! - If 0 chunks and 0 options changed, linking returns [`LinkMode.Skipped`] with zero file writes.
//! - If only Silk functions or supported static data objects changed (same-size/padded rewrites,
//!   grown functions relocated into `__text` headroom with 12-byte thunk updates, moved private
//!   `<fn>.constant.<N>` objects, new bump-allocated `__DATA` pointer-bearing objects threaded
//!   into `LC_DYLD_CHAINED_FIXUPS`, removed ordinary functions, or in-place `silk_seen` updates),
//!   [`MachOIncremental`] creates an APFS CoW clone (`clonefile`), `pwrite`s ONLY the dirty byte
//!   ranges, recomputes ONLY the dirty 4 KB SHA-256 page hashes inside `LC_CODE_SIGNATURE`, sets
//!   mode `0755`, and atomically renames the fresh vnode over `output`.
//! - Never mutates an already-executed Mach-O inode in place, preventing XNU per-vnode
//!   code-signature cache kills (`SIGKILL` / `Killed: 9`) on Apple Silicon.
//! - Falls back transparently to a clean full [`MachOLink.linkWithOptions`] build whenever
//!   headroom, thunk slots, TLS, dynamic imports, or debug options require layout changes.

